{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Moreover, you have not brought us to a land flowing with milk and honey.</b> He says: You took us out from a good place; had you brought us to a place as good as it and given us fields and vineyards as we had in Egypt, and you sought to rule over us — we would have endured it. But you took us out from our fields and vineyards and did not bring us to a place like it, and if so, why do you rule?" "<b>Will you put out the eyes of those men?</b> If you punish us by putting out eyes, we will not go up. And in his saying האנשים ההם ('those men') he used a euphemism, for it should have been said העינינו ('our eyes')." "<b>And there is one</b> who explained: He was willing to have the eyes of those men put out so that they would not see, and he said האנשים ההם ('those men') referring to those who went out of Egypt, as if they said: We are willing to have their eyes put out so that they will not see, for certainly this thing you did is clearly visible to the eyes — and it is like the parable of an ordinary person that people say: So-and-so's eyes are shut, therefore he does not see." "<b>And behold,</b> the wicked — their mouth caused them to stumble at the beginning and at the end. At the beginning of their words it was folly, for they began by saying 'we will not go up'; and at the end of their words too they concluded with 'we will not go up.'" "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> העיני האנשים ההם תנקר לא נעלה — it is not written 'we will not go' (לא נלך), it is not written 'we will not prophesy' (לא נבא), but rather 'we will not go up' (לא נעלה). (Proverbs 18:7) ״פי כסיל מחתה לו״ — they opened their mouths for destruction, saying they would die by descent and not by ascent; just as they said, so they died."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:05.808827674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}